# ripgrep-only ignore file (honored by rg and the Claude Code Grep tool).
#
# This is NOT .gitignore — every file listed here is still tracked, still built,
# and still deployed. It only keeps large generated/data blobs out of repo-wide
# CONTENT SEARCHES, where a single incidental match can dump hundreds of KB.
#
# All of these remain directly readable by exact path (Read, jq, cat) — the only
# thing that changes is that a broad `grep` sweep no longer walks them.
#
# If you genuinely need to search one of these, pass it explicitly:
#   rg --no-ignore -F "<term>" scripts/www/cgi-bin/quecmanager/operator-list.json

# 415 KB carrier/PLMN lookup table shipped to the device. Consulted by exact key,
# never by full-text search.
scripts/www/cgi-bin/quecmanager/operator-list.json

# 498 KB single-path SVG. Text, so ripgrep will happily search it and return one
# unreadable multi-hundred-KB line.
public/device-icon.svg

# Lockfile. Use `bun pm ls` / `bun why` rather than grepping it.
bun.lock

# Binary deps are auto-skipped by ripgrep's binary detection; listed for the
# reader's benefit, not because rg needs the hint.
dependencies/atcli_smd11
dependencies/sms_tool
